WEBVTT

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:03.350
This is the challenger's chance!

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.850
Whoa, but it's a punch that barely taps against the guard!

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.900
Does he not have the strength to fight back!?

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.770
No!

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.560
He was gauging the distance!

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.370
<i>A twisting punch?</i>

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.530
<i>The corkscrew blow?</i>

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.160
The champion's guarding his head! 

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.200
His heart's wide open!

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.160
The perfect scenario...

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.160
Go!

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.920
Heartbreak Shot!

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.940
An elbow block!

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:57.610
What was that!?

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.190
Date cried out all of a sudden!

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.200
Eiji!

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.070
It's the worst thing that could've happened!

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.420
I don't know if he saw it coming or if it was reflexive, but...

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.070
he avoided the old man's biggest shot!

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:10.530
Not only that, but he just drilled his hand into that hard and pointy elbow.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.080
Without a doubt, the old man's fist is shattered.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.750
Forget the Heartbreak Shot.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.090
He won't even be able to throw regular punches now.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.160
<i>To think you had that kind of strength left.</i>

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.590
<i>But, it's a shame.</i>

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:25.950
<i>You showed your trump card, and it was still ineffective.</i>

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.350
<i>You've got nothing left.</i>

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.520
The champion continues his surging rush!

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.230
Will he be able to finish it!?

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.730
Amazing...

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.540
<i>Is it over?</i>

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.160
<i>Is there nothing left he can do?</i>

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.240
<i>To think that the wall around the world title was so high</i>

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.240
<i>that even Date-san... couldn't reach it. {may need re-timing}</i>

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.020
<i>My mouth is full of blood.</i>

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.750
<i>Did I break a tooth?</i>

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:02.210
<i>No...</i>

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.740
<i>my tongue isn't touching anything.</i>

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.970
<i>He broke my jaw!</i>

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.080
<i>He got my ribs too.</i>

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:11.850
<i>And to top it off...</i>

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.350
<i>the joints in my right hand are broken.</i>

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:19.850
<i>He's taken away everything that I needed to win.</i>

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:20.910
<i>No,</i>

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:24.360
<i>I might've never had a chance to begin with.</i>

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.050
<i>I guess I can't beat him after all.</i>

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.370
<i>No matter how many times I fight him.</i>

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.020
<i>I...</i>

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.060
Stop!

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.170
<i>I survived.</i>

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:41.630
<i>But...</i>

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.620
<i>why did I bother?</i>

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:49.140
<i>I don't have any weapons left to fight with.</i>

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.140
<i>I-It's...  {may need re-timing}</i>

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.460
Eiji...

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.400
It's enough, isn't it?

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.750
There's no one who could have made it this far!

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.900
It's enough, right!?

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.410
<i>Enough?</i>

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.830
<i>That's right.</i>

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.090
<i>I'm out of weapons.</i>

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.660
<i>I don't even know why I should bother standing up.</i>

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.420
<i>If I can't win... If I don't have any chance...</i>

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:29.070
<i>then I might as well...</i>

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:53.320
Please wash this off.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:54.700
R-Right.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.030
Honey, just a little more!

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.460
There are only three rounds left!

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:04.210
We'll watch over you until the very end!

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:05.810
Until the end...

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.550
Pops...

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:27.520
C-Coach...

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.680
Keep quiet!

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:35.330
I guess it's not enough for you yet, Eiji.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.200
Win...

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.210
What's that? I can't hear you.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:40.930
Win...

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.130
I'll win.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.090
Well, if you can still say something like that, there's no reason to stop you.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:51.150
Coach...

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:54.220
If he can still move even a finger, he'll keep at it.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.340
We've been through a lot together.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.310
Go get it done, Eiji.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.730
Are they still going to fight?

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:06.080
From a second's perspective, I question whether or not they should let him continue fighting.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.050
There's no point in continuing.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:09.350
Bill...

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:12.090
This is boxing.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:15.460
There's no telling what could happen next.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.190
As long as he stays standing,

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:19.930
there's always the possibility that a miracle could occur.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.000
Seconds out! {jama: added}

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.500
My job is

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.910
to lower that possibility to zero.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.130
Even if that means

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:32.960
Eiji Date becomes an "unfortunate accident."

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:35.980
Mama, how is Papa?

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.570
Is he okay?

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.740
Just watch until the end.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:41.310
Okay. {jama: added}

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.690
<i>I thought I was going to stop him.</i>

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:49.070
<i>I thought I wanted him to stop.</i>

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.400
<i>But...</i>

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.030
<i>when I saw his eyes, I couldn't bring myself to say the words.</i>

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:56.670
<i>If he had stopped there,</i>

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:59.040
<i>everything would have gone back to the way things were seven years ago.</i>

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:03.950
<i>For him, this fight is how he can regain his sense of self.</i>

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:06.130
<i>All we can do is watch...</i>

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.410
<i>and wait.</i>

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:11.540
<i>So that he can really be himself when he comes back.</i>

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:13.960
We're heading into the tenth round now!

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.550
Does the challenger have enough strength left to turn this around?

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:18.480
Both fighters head out from their corners.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.700
Date-san, show him your spirit!

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:22.530
Only three rounds left!

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:25.060
Ippo, you say something too, damn it!

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.600
<i>That's right... That's all I can do.</i>

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:28.750
<i>Cheer him on!</i>

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.030
Date-san!

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.960
You can still do it!

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.320
The champion is exhausted too!

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.890
That's right, Date!

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:37.180
We believe in you!

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:40.330
We came to see you become the champion!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:49.330
A "Date" chant shakes the Kokugikan as it comes down to these final moments!

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.230
The challenger answers the cheers by taking the offensive!

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:52.590
Left! Another left!

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:55.990
Will the challenger be able to survive this round!?

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:57.200
He's still got some speed left!

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.340
That's a good left!

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:00.910
His right's broken!

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:02.610
All he has is his left!

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.050
The champion's figured it out too.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:06.850
He's not worried about a right at all.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:12.170
<i>I know your right fist is broken,</i>

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:15.530
<i>and just dodging your left is nothing.</i>

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:21.790
<i>I'll throw a counter against this left and that will be the end.</i>

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:35.050
A right!

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:36.230
What!?

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:38.050
H-He threw a right!

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:41.960
The champion's expression shows more shock than pain!

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.120
He's stopped moving!

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.310
The challenger moves forward!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:47.450
It becomes an inspiration for earth-shaking cheers!

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:50.310
The challenger is on the offensive!

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.600
<i>Your right fist is broken.</i>

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:54.070
<i>How can you still attack?</i>

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.080
<i>I've remembered...</i>

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.290
<i>why I'm still standing.</i>

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.860
<i>The reason I'm fighting!</i>

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:03.850
Can we get a comment?

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.580
Any words on your plans for the future?

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.870
Does she not want an autograph?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.590
Aiko just came along because we asked her to.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.590
Her name is Aiko, huh?

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:24.090
What'd you think?

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.600
I was great in today's match, right!?

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:31.870
I-I don't really know.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:36.110
It's so scary watching you box.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:38.930
Listen up!

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:40.860
I've got big news! Don't be too shocked, okay?

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:42.890
The world title!

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:45.830
My world title match has finally been decided!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.560
It's finally come!

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.660
Now I can finally show you...

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.310
that I'm the best in the world!

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:54.290
I promise, I'll show you!

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:02.550
This might not be a good time to tell you about my news then.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:04.550
Did you say something?

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:07.250
No. {jama: added - shortened by Puar}

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:10.390
Good luck, Eiji-san!

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:11.560
<i>That's right.</i>

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.150
<i>I wanted to show Aiko...</i>

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.810
<i>how cool I am!</i>

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:19.370
<i>Looking good in front of my woman...</i>

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:21.150
<i>It might not be an impressive dream,</i>

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:24.570
<i>but to me, it's the most important thing!</i>

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:26.080
<i>That's</i>

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:30.080
<i>what makes me who I am!</i>

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:34.080
<i>He still won't go down?</i>

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.420
<i>I want to win!</i>

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.340
<i>I've got to look good for her!</i>

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.050
<i>There's no way I can back off looking this pathetic!</i>

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:47.160
<i>I can feel his bones are broken.</i>

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:48.800
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.850
<i>At this rate, Eiji Date really will become an unfortunate accident.</i>

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:53.050
Ricardo!

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:54.490
What are you hesitating for!?

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:55.860
He's still standing!

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:00.860
A left!

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:04.140
The champion is off balance!

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:06.330
He's twisting his right.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.120
He's gonna use it!

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.620
The Heartbreak Shot!

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:13.360
<i>You can break all the bones you want.</i>

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.290
<i>But in exchange,</i>

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:17.630
<i>I'll take your</i>

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.890
<i>life!</i>

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:33.890
<i>It made it through!</i>

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:36.550
The Heartbreak Shot!

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:39.900
His trump card explodes!

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.400
Ricardo!

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:45.230
The champion's time...

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:45.900
...has stopped!

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:48.160
A full power left.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.160
He'll get a free shot!

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:52.410
Get him, Eiji!

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:54.640
<i>He can't dodge this left.</i>

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.080
<i>It'll land!</i>

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:57.660
<i>Date-san will win!</i>

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.670
<i>Aiko...</i>

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:03.420
<i>are you watching?</i>

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:05.420
<i>I'm back!</i>

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:07.170
<i>This is who I am.</i>

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:10.040
<i>Date Eiji!</i>

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:29.390
<i>W-Why?</i>

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:37.620
<i>Aiko...</i>

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:39.370
<i>are you watching?</i>

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.380
<i>I'm back!</i>

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.130
<i>This is who I am.</i>

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:46.210
<i>Date Eiji!</i>

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:03.380
<i>W-Why?</i>

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:13.660
<i>How sad, Eiji Date.</i>

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:17.160
<i>Your speed and timing were both perfect.</i>

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:21.280
<i>Had your power matched them...</i>

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:24.610
<i>I might have been frozen in time.</i>

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:29.020
<i>If your right fist hadn't been broken, you might have been able to cut me down.</i>

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:32.560
<i>From now on, when I'm asked...</i>

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:36.460
<i>which boxer I respect the most,</i>

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:39.460
<i>I'll answer...</i>

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:42.900
<i>He lives on an island nation in the Pacific,</i>

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:46.270
<i>a samurai that I met in Japan.</i>

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:49.280
The champion's right!

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:51.280
<i>We'll never</i>

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:53.530
<i>meet in the ring again,</i>

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:56.790
<i>but I will never forget your name.</i>

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:00.580
Please dodge it,

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.000
Date-san!

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:06.590
Damn... it...

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:33.590
<i>Goodbye,</i>

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:36.320
<i>Eiji Date.</i>

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:53.390
The match is over!

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:55.890
With this final down, the referee crosses his arms!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:14:00.180
The championship does not change hands in this WBA World Featherweight Title Match!

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.100
Round 10, 2 minutes and 14 seconds!

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:06.750
Japan's Date shatters against the legendary champion!

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:08.730
S-Stretcher! Get a stretcher!

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:11.190
Hey... Date's not moving...

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:13.540
Not good... The way he fell was bad.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:14.700
Date!

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:19.470
The Mexican flag is raised amidst the silent arena!

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:20.950
D-Date-san...

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:24.460
The champion was indeed mighty!

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:30.000
But the man who faced the legendary champion head on deserves our applause!

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:31.360
Thank you!

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:33.230
Thank you, Date Eiji!

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:35.540
You did great, Date!

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.330
You moved me, man!

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:02.330
"I've never faced a boxer so brave and spirited."

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:06.350
"Eiji Date was a magnificent challenger."

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:08.330
That's just a bunch of polite lip service.

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:10.950
Did you see the champion's face after the match?

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:12.130
Not a scratch on him.

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:16.590
To think that Date-san would lose so shockingly...

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:20.410
Multiple broken ribs, his lower jaw had numerous fractures,

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:23.510
and his right hand was broken clear through to the wrist.

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:26.140
It's impressive that he was still able to fight like that.

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:28.070
He was so close.

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.840
If only that last right had worked.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:31.070
Give it up already.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:32.610
What's done is done.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:34.870
The old man did a great job.

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:37.900
He lived up to his role as the supreme challenger.

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:40.040
However, things still ended up like this.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:48.460
I don't think the WBA Featherweight Belt is going anywhere until Ricardo Martinez retires.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:51.340
What do you think Date-san is going to do now?

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:55.300
He was hurt pretty bad and, even after he's healed, if you consider his age...

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:57.260
Well, he'll probably reti-

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:05.310
Please.

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:07.080
Just...

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:08.350
don't say anything else.

00:16:08.350 --> 00:16:09.620
Ippo... {jama: added}

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:11.310
Oh, you're all here.

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:13.020
Date's regained consciousness.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:17.880
Thankfully, in spite of all that happened, there's no brain damage.

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:21.280
They're going to keep an eye out for symptoms, but it looks like there won't be anything life threatening.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:22.540
Is that right?

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.310
After the way he fell, thank goodness.

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:26.510
That's a relief.

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:29.290
Can the old man talk?

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:34.790
Well, he seemed to be talking to his family, so maybe if it's just for a short while...

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:36.750
Get going.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:39.750
B-But...

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:41.900
I can't think of anything to say.

00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:45.340
I wouldn't know what to say...

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:47.400
or what to ask him.

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:50.310
You should still go.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:54.760
There's a meaning...

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.320
to you seeing him.

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:00.010
Come on,

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:01.220
I'll drive you there.

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:03.320
I'll go get changed.

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:23.690
<i>I had already noticed it.</i>

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:27.770
<i>Since the match against Makunouchi-san,</i>

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:30.600
<i>the scar on your nose had stopped aching.</i>

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:32.600
<i>Yes...</i>

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:37.900
<i>You had already regained your identity.</i>

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:43.000
<i>I wasn't able to say it back then, but...</i>

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.680
<i>seeing you full of confidence again made me so happy!</i>

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:48.910
<i>So proud!</i>

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.690
<i>And now I can finally say it...</i>

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:54.930
Welcome home...

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:56.140
Eiji-san.

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:05.380
Excuse me.

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:07.300
Um...

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:10.300
I heard Date-san had regained consciousness, so...

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:12.890
Honey,

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:15.330
Makunouchi-san is here.

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:16.640
Do you understand me?

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:18.090
Maku... nou...

00:18:18.420 --> 00:18:19.270
D-Date-san!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:22.490
I-It's fine, don't try to talk!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:23.820
I'll leave right away!

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:31.080
Maku... nouchi...

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.080
My... hand...

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:39.070
Take... it...

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.910
W-What is it?

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:44.590
What should I do with your hand?

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:46.820
Do you want me to grab it?

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:48.510
But the fractures...

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:54.100
Baton...

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:56.000
pass.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:19:00.110
It's... yours now.

00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:13.190
Makunouchi-san,

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:15.220
he still needs his rest.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:16.850
So for today...

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:17.730
Right.

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:19.840
Well, take care.

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:23.130
Mister!

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:25.870
You're the Japanese Champion, right?

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:29.360
You're the one who's going to challenge that guy next, right!?

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:32.820
You'll get revenge for Papa, right!?

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:37.390
I'm sorry.

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:39.890
I can't do it.

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:43.170
Ricardo Martinez is too strong.

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:44.400
As I am now,

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:46.830
I wouldn't stand a chance.

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:01.890
That guy's a weakling!

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:03.650
And a coward!

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:06.410
If I was bigger...

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:07.670
Yuji,

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:10.490
weren't you listening?

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:13.390
Makunouchi-san...

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:24.040
Makunouchi-san said...

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:28.220
that he can't <i>as he is now.</i>
